    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11461" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">crassāmentum</span></b> , i, n.
		id. (post-Aug.), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the thickness</i> of an object. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">portarum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					16, 40, 77, § 210</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">surculi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					17, 9, 7</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Esp., <i>the thick sediment of a liquid, the dregs,
				grounds</i>, <i><span class="en">Col. 12, 12, 1</span></i>.</div>
